% The gchord codes g, h, i, j, k play the notes of a guitar chord from the
% lowest, which in an inversion such as "C/E" is the bass note (GitHub
% issue #11).  configure_gchord() (genmidi.c) raised the notes below the
% bass note by an octave but kept them in the order of the chord
% definition, so that g played the root: "C/E" with ghih played C' G E G
% instead of E G C' G.  A bass note that is not in the chord, as in "C/B",
% leaves the chord unchanged.  In "C9/E" and "C9/Bb" the raised root comes
% before the ninth, D'.
X:1
T:Gchord codes on inverted chords
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/2
Q:1/4=120
K:C
%%MIDI gchord ghih
"C"CE|"C/E"EG|"C/G"Gc|"Am/C"CE|"Am/E"EA|"C/B"B,C|
%%MIDI gchord ghij
"G7"B,D|"G7/B"B,D|"G7/D"DF|"G7/F"FG|
%%MIDI gchord hijk
"C9"CE|"C9/E"EG|"C9/Bb"_BG|
%%MIDI gchord GHIH
"C/E"EG|]
